Rule links in the phase tree (Graph → Business rules and Simulation → Reasoning)

Context: rule names in the Graph → Business rules tree and the Simulation →
Reasoning tree were plain text. Users wanted to open a rule and edit it without
leaving the page. The rule editors (IF-THEN graph editor for Simple rules, SPARQL
editor for Complex rules) live on the Ontology page, which loads ontology-core.js
and runs page-level setup. That script cannot run on Graph or Simulation, so the
editor scripts are loaded on demand instead. The editor partial is included
server-side in a hidden #if-then-section on both pages. Editing follows the
Ontology rules: only users with ontology edit rights can save; others see the
rule read-only. After Save, the list refreshes in place, ticked rules stay
ticked, and the editor closes. No OWL regeneration is needed.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/global/js/phase-tree.js
   Rule titles render as links (`ob-tree-rule-link`) when the item has `link`.
   `fromNamedRules` sets `link: true`. A click emits `ob:rule-open` with
   `{key, value}` and does not toggle the checkbox.
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-if-then.js
   Editor DOM bindings moved into `IfThenModule.bindEditorDom()` (idempotent).
   New `IfThenModule.initStandalone()` for use outside the Ontology page.
   `saveRule` dispatches `ob:rules-saved` with `{key: 'if_then'}`.
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js
   New `BusinessRulesModule.initStandalone()`. `sparqlOpenEditor(index, {readOnly})`
   opens the Complex editor read-only (fields, assistant and validate disabled,
   Save hidden). The editor is re-enabled on close. `_saveRule` dispatches
   `ob:rules-saved` with `{key: ruleType}`.
4. src/front/static/global/js/rule-editor-loader.js (new)
   `RuleEditorLoader`: loads the editor CSS and JS once, in order, then runs the
   standalone init. `open(key, name, {canEdit})` opens the right editor. If the
   rule no longer exists, it shows a warning and refreshes the list. `attach(tree,
   root)` wires a PhaseTree to `ob:rule-open` and `ob:rules-saved`, and refreshes
   the list while keeping the selection. The asset version comes from the
   `data-asset-version` attribute on the script tag (no inline script, per the
   page contract tests).
5. src/front/templates/dtwin.html
   Hidden `#if-then-section` wrapper with the business-rules editor partial,
   inside the reasoning section. `rule-editor-loader.js` added after `phase-tree.js`.
6. src/front/templates/simulation.html
   Same wrapper inside the Reasoning workbench, and the loader script added before
   `simulation-rules.js`.
7. src/front/static/query/js/query-reasoning.js
   Calls `RuleEditorLoader.attach(this._tree, root)` after creating the tree.
8. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-rules.js
   Calls `RuleEditorLoader.attach(this._tree, root)` after creating the tree.
9. tests/units/front/test_rule_links_contract.py (new)
   Contract tests: link rendering and event, standalone init and idempotent
   binding, read-only Complex editor, `ob:rules-saved` on both save paths, loader
   asset list (no ontology-core.js), page wiring and script order, and no ID
   clashes between the editor partial and the Inference / Simulation pages.
10. docs/user-guide.md
    Graph → Business rules and Simulation → Reasoning sections: rule links,
    read-only behaviour, and refresh after save.
11. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-rule-links-in-phase-tree-design.md and
    docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-10-rule-links-in-phase-tree.md (new)
    Design and implementation plan for this change.

