Rules export / import, separate from the OWL

Context: Simple (IF-THEN) rules were written into the generated OWL as
ontobricks:IfThenRule annotations, so moving rules between domains meant moving
OWL. Rules are now managed as their own versioned JSON file: one export with all
Simple and Complex rules, one import with upsert by name and per-rule validation.
The generated OWL no longer contains Simple rules. OWL import still reads rules
from files that carry the old annotations. No OWL regeneration is involved.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
   Removed the IF-THEN emission loop and `_add_if_then_rule`. The `if_then_rules`
   constructor argument is kept, so callers are unchanged.
2. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   - `save_if_then_rule` uses `Rules.validate_if_then_rule` (one validator for the
     save route and the import route); errors are joined with "; ".
   - New `GET /ontology/rules/export`: attachment `<domain>_rules.json`.
   - New `POST /ontology/rules/import`: parses the body (non-JSON gives a 4xx),
     applies the package, saves the domain, records change-audit events with the
     same actions as the single-rule routes (if_then_added/updated,
     sparql_rules_added/updated), and returns added / replaced / rejected.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/RulesPackage.py (new)
   Pure functions: `build_package`, `apply_package` (header check, upsert by name,
   per-rule validation: Simple via `Rules.validate_if_then_rule`, enabled Complex
   via `SPARQLRuleEngine.validate_rule`). Disabled Complex rules are not compiled,
   so a legacy rule can still be exported and re-imported.
4. src/back/objects/ontology/ImportResult.py (new)
   Dataclass with the merged lists, added / replaced / rejected and the change tuples.
   Its own file, one public class per file (architecture rule). Re-exported from
   `back/objects/ontology/__init__.py`.
5. src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html
   Header controls before "Add Rule": "Export rules" (link), "Import rules"
   (button, class ontology-edit-btn) and a hidden file input.
6. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js
   `importRulesFile` (JSON parse, not-a-rules-file checks, confirmation, POST,
   refresh of both lists and badges), `_showImportSummary` (Added / Replaced /
   Rejected modal), and the import action and file-change listener in
   `_bindBrStaticUiOnce`.
7. tests/units/ontology/test_owl_generator.py, test_workflow_owl_roundtrip.py
   Assert that Simple rules are no longer written to the OWL (the round-trip now
