Fix empty compare-graph image in Simulation Evaluate report
===========================================================

Context: Simulation → Compare → Evaluate report showed the comparison
graph as an empty warm square. Sigma.js WebGL layers use
``preserveDrawingBuffer: false``, and the report opened from the Evaluate
tab while the Graphs pane was ``display:none``, so a live canvas composite
read a cleared buffer.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-compare.js
   Snapshot the layered canvases into ``lastGraphPng`` in the same turn as
   ``renderer.refresh()`` (and on resize). Clear the snapshot on teardown /
   failed compare.
2. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-evaluate.js
   Report graph image uses ``SimulationCompare.lastGraphPng`` instead of
   re-reading hidden WebGL canvases.
3. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
   Contract: snapshot after refresh; evaluate report consumes the cache.

