Fix compare-graph report image still blank (hidden-pane overwrite)
==================================================================

Context: the cached compare-graph snapshot was still an empty square. Sigma
renders a hidden container at 1x1 (``allowInvalidContainer``); switching to
the Evaluate tab fired the ResizeObserver, which re-snapshotted the 1x1 blank
over the good image. Reproduced headless: same-turn snapshot after refresh
has the graph, a later read has labels only, a hidden read is 1x1.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-compare.js
   ``_snapshotGraphPng`` skips (keeps the last snapshot) when the canvas
   container is smaller than 2px, runs a synchronous ``renderer.refresh()``
   right before the WebGL read, and ignores 1x1 layers.
2. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
   Contract: hidden-pane guard, refresh-before-drawImage, 1x1 filter.

